name: sim.unpackFloatTable
description: Unpacks a string (or part of it) into an array of floating-point numbers
luaSynopsis: list floatingNumbers = sim.unpackFloatTable(bytes data, int startFloatIndex = 0, int floatCount = 0, int additionalByteOffset = 0)
pythonSynopsis: float[] floatingNumbers = sim.unpackFloatTable(buffer data, int startFloatIndex = 0, int floatCount = 0, int additionalByteOffset = 0)
inputs:
1. data: string (values between 0 and 255) that contains packed floating-point numbers
2. startFloatIndex: zero-based index from which on data should be unpacked (from data[4*startFloatIndex+1+additionalByteOffset]). Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. floatCount: amount of floats that should be unpacked. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum of floats should be unpacked from the indicated startFloatIndex)
4. additionalByteOffset: byte offset that will be added before reading the floats. Can be omitted, in which case 0 is used.
outputs:
1. floatingNumbers: array containing unpacked floating-point numbers
